[size=14pt][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]0.6.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[b]New features[/b]
[list]
[li]Added a hyperspace map. If you keep scrolling out past the minimum zoom, the view glides out to a map of every region's main star.[/li]
[li]Added smart respec. Ctrl+Shift+click an allocated node to remove it and every node that depends on it, one at a time at auto-allocate's pace, farthest first, with the clicked node last. Doing this on the starting point clears the tree and returns you to the starting point choice. A click or Escape cancels a respec in progress. It does nothing if any node it would remove has its own removal condition.[/li]
[li]The starting root can now be chosen again. While it is the only allocated node, click it to undo the choice.[/li]
[li]Added Lost Sector themed areas to the skill tree (with permission). These new areas are optional, with direct ports of some Kesteven hullmods and some thematic designs of my own.
[list]
[li]Auto shows it only when Lost Sector is installed, and On and Off in Lunalib override that.[/li]
[li]Switching an area off removes its nodes from every ship and refunds their OP, banked allocations and item costs. The change applies on the next save load.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]The refit screen has a new Skill Tree button (hotkey K) one slot below Build In. With Ship Mastery System installed, it sits directly under the Mastery button. This replaces the old button to open the skill tree.[/li]
[li]The Exiled Sector Skill Tree hull mod is now visible in the refit screen.
[list]
[li]Hovering it lists an aggregate of every bonus from the ship's allocated nodes, up to 25 lines plus a count of the rest.[/li]
[li]Clicking its icon opens the skill tree.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]Nodes that copy a vanilla hull mod now place the real hull mod on the ship as a phantom.
[list]
[li]The phantom is permanent, costs 0 OP and does nothing by itself, but other mods that check for that hull mod see it.[/li]
[li]High Resolution Sensors and Phase Field are the exceptions.[/li]
[li]Phantoms are hidden from the refit screen's installed hull mod lists and from ships' Codex related entries, and their tooltip names the node that provides them. They still appear as hullmods in some areas.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]Multipliers from the skill tree ("% more / % less") now add together instead of compounding.
[list]
[li]For example, 2% + 2% more is now 4% more, and 15% more plus 30% less is 15% less. The total never goes past 100% less.[/li]
[li]Temporary nodes still apply their own multiplier that can compound.[/li]
[li]The X panel summary adds them the same way and hides multipliers that cancel out.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]Added drastically improved NPC fleet generation logic, introducing themed randomness to all NPC fleets.[/li]
[li]Node tooltips now show only the description, effects and temporary duration.
[list]
[li]Press F1 in the skill tree to show or hide the rest: mutual exclusivity, hull requirements, hull sizes, item cost, deallocation warnings and the free-node note.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[/list]

[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[li]Lost Sector (tested with 0.6.2d) is optional.
[list]
[li]With it installed, the Kesteven and Frozen Heart areas appear, controlled by the Optional Areas setting.[/li]
[li]Kesteven nodes place Lost Sector's own hull mods as phantoms.[/li]
[li]On hulls with Augmented Systems, these nodes give the same extra bonuses as Lost Sector's hull mods. Volatile Flux Injector's high-flux penalties are halved, and Inertial Supercharger also raises projectile speed by its damage bonus.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]Second-in-Command changes:
[list]
[li]It now sees the real Shield Shunt and Safety Overrides hull mods through their phantoms, so its own Redistribution and Enhanced Overrides bonuses apply.[/li]
[li]The tree's "counts as" stand-in lines are gone.[/li]
[li]It also sees Militarized Subsystems as installed.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]MagicLib: when another hull mod tries to strip one of a node's phantom hull mods through MagicLib, that hull mod is removed instead.[/li]
[li]Ship Mastery System and other mods that check for Safety Overrides now see it on ships with the node.[/li]
[li]The skill tree hull mod now applies after every other hull mod, including D-mods and Second-in-Command's controller, so crew-based effects see the final values.[/li]
[li]Split-beam and refraction drones now copy marker hull mods from the firing ship.
[list]
[li]This makes ET-IX's Dawnstar and Daythorn beams, and the misfire checks of ET-IX and Emergent Threats beams, work on drones.[/li]
[li]The list is in data/config/exiledSector/drone_marker_hullmods.csv, which merges across mods.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]The beam split and refraction blocklists were re-checked against the new drones.
[list]
[li]The Repulser, the energy ball launcher and the Supernova now refract normally, so the refraction blocklist is empty.[/li]
[li]Devastator, Whiplash, Limited Ammo, SBE, Fermion Decoupler, Electrolaser Pulse and Destiny Spear beams now split normally.[/li]
[li]Six beam effects stay blocked.[/li]
[/list][/li]
[li]At startup, starsector.log gets a self-check line for Lost Sector, Second-in-Command and MagicLib. It says whether each mod is absent, at the tested version, at an untested version, or missing something Exiled Sector relies on.[/li]
[li]The mod no longer ships a copy of vanilla's Orbitron 20 bold font, which broke campaign UI text alongside font or localisation mods.[/li]
[/list]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed Refracting Projectiles crashing combat on some modded projectiles. Refracted shots also no longer appear on the shield they just hit, or break on special projectiles.[/li]
[li]Fixed Lion's Gaze split-beam drones staying in battle forever after the firing ship retreated or its wreck was removed.[/li]
[li]Fixed a crash on loading a save, caused by the tree changing hull mods during the game's OP-cost calculation.[/li]
[li]Fixed Fighter Replacement nodes speeding up fighter replacement rate decay instead of slowing it.[/li]
[li]Fixed Phase Anchor's emergency dive trying to trigger on ships without a phase cloak.[/li]
[li]Fixed XP not being awarded for auto-resolved pursuits.[/li]
[li]Fixed captured NPC ships losing their skill tree when another fight followed straight away.[/li]
[li]Fixed two one-way links in the tree. They now unlock from either end.[/li]
[li]Choice nodes whose chosen option no longer exists, or is no longer offered, are now removed and refunded on load. A skill type that fails to load no longer changes saves.[/li]
[li]Choice nodes are now checked against the restrictions of both the node and the chosen option, everywhere.[/li]
[li]Nodes removed from the tree, or from a switched-off area, now also refund their item cost.[/li]
[li]Tooltip tables now use the current root's accent colour instead of the colour they were first drawn with.[/li]
[li]Raised the limit on ships that can hold paid skill tree nodes at the same time from 1,000 to 10,000.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[b]0.5.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[li]You can now save a ship's skill tree as a named template and load it onto any other ship with the same starting node. A loaded template shows its path as green connectors, and the Auto-allocate button fills it in for you, skipping any nodes that are blocked or cost items.[/li]
[li]Ships now earn more XP from harder fights, using the same difficulty rating vanilla shows before combat. It only ever adds XP, the post-battle report tells you how much, and you can adjust its strength and cap in LunaLib.[/li]
[li]Improved allocation animations[/li]
[li]If a future update removes nodes from the tree, your ships get back the OP and free allocations they spent on them. If a ship's starting root is removed, its tree is reset so you can pick a new one, and it keeps its level, XP and banked allocations. Hopefully this makes skill tree iterations not break your saves.[/li]
[/list]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[li]Nodes could end up costing no OP. The hidden hull mods that reserve OP for skill nodes leaked until they ran out, and after that new ships reserved nothing.[/li]
[li]A giant stretched ship hull could sometimes appear across the skill tree (the HOUND bug).[/li]
[li]Skills that add OP to every ship in the fleet only counted toward the flagship's skill tree budget. They now count for every ship.[/li]
[li]Nodes allocated on a ship you had just bought could give no bonuses and reserve no OP. Not 100% sure this is fixed yet.[/li]
[li]Pressing Escape in the search box closed the whole panel; now it just clears the search.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[b]0.4.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[b]New features[/b]
[list]
[li]Some nodes are now limited to certain hull sizes, like their vanilla hull mods.[/li]
[li]New split notables for things like Expanded Magazines.[/li]
[li]Balance changes to several nodes.[/li]
[li]Massive improvements to performance.[/li]
[/list]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed nodes allocated right after choosing a starting point costing no OP.[/li]
[li]Missile Autoloader and Neural Interface nodes now work in combat.[/li]
[li]Shared Fate and High Scatter Amp now work as described.[/li]
[li]Shield Shunt can no longer be taken on phase ships or unshielded ships.[/li]
[li]UI and tooltip fixes.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[b]0.3.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[li]First draft Simplified Chinese translation of the whole mod. Node search also matches English names and ids, so you can still search while playing in Chinese.[/li]
[li]Other languages can now be added more easily.[/li]
[/list]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed a crash to desktop when opening the NPC Scaling tab in the LunaLib settings.[/li]
[li]Fixed the post-battle salvage bonus not dropping after the ship or node providing it was lost, sold or removed.[/li]
[li]Terrifying Presence's enemy accuracy penalty now shows in green, since it helps you.[/li]
[li]Very small numbers no longer display in scientific notation (e.g. 1.0E-4).[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[b]0.2.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[b]New features[/b]
[list]
[li]The first time you open a ship's skill tree, you now pick where it starts: Low Tech, Midline or High Tech. The choice is permanent, but the other two starting points can still be reached later. They just cost OP like any other node.[/li]
[li]NPC fleets now have skill trees too. Officers' ships, flagships and a share of the other ships in every faction's fleets get their own trees, and that includes your own faction's fleets and your allies. How developed they are scales with your character level.[/li]
[li]There are nine NPC builds, three for each starting point, and each one is fitted to the ship it's on. A shieldless hull never gets a shield build, carrier nodes only go on ships with fighter bays, and anything a ship can't use is skipped.[/li]
[li]When an NPC ship has a hullmod that matches a skill node, it swaps the hullmod out for the node and spends the freed OP on extra nodes.[/li]
[li]There's a new "NPC Scaling" tab in the LunaLib settings.[/li]
[li]You can inspect NPC skill trees by pressing X (rebindable) during a fleet encounter or while hovering over a fleet on the map. It shows which ships have trees, along with their build, level, key nodes and combined bonuses.[/li]
[li]Pressing F2 on a ship's tooltip now opens an "Exiled Sector skill tree" entry in the Codex with the same summary.[/li]
[li]Recovered NPC ships keep their skill tree as their own. They don't get Reinforced Bulkheads' near-guaranteed recovery, though, so levelled enemies aren't free loot.[/li]
[li]You can zoom out twice as far on the skill tree screen.[/li]
[/list]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed a crash when playing alongside Second-in-Command.[/li]
[li]Notable nodes now dim like other nodes when unallocated, when filtered out by search, and while the tree fades in. They were always drawn at full brightness.[/li]
[li]Notable node rings and wormhole glows now render with the intended glow instead of looking flat.[/li]
[li]The breathing glow on nodes you can allocate is twice as bright, so available nodes are easier to spot.[/li]
[li]The solar corona and hyperspace storm resistance tooltip now correctly reads "X% less combat readiness loss", instead of describing its multiplier as a flat decrease.[/li]
[li]Removed a hullmod blueprint tooltip line meant to point to the matching skill node, which never actually appeared.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[b]0.1.0[/b]
[spoiler]
[list]
[li]Initial release.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]
